## What Is Wireless Penetration Testing?

Wireless penetration testing is a cybersecurity assessment that evaluates the security of Wi-Fi networks through authorized testing techniques. Security professionals examine wireless access points, encryption protocols, authentication methods, network configurations, and access controls to identify weaknesses before malicious attackers can exploit them.

This process helps businesses understand their wireless security risks and implement effective protection measures.

